\f1\tab\f0 The TRAN program was used \f1 to support \f0 the first\f1  \f0 application of \f1\tab\f0 the\f1  \f0 Inter\f1 P\f0 rocessor Buffer [IPB] dual-bus asynchronous transfer \f1\tab\f0 device.  A \f1 PDP-8 \f0 with a high-speed reader provide\f1 d\f0  BIN loader \f1\tab\f0 support to a\f1 nother PDP-8\f0  with only a\f1  T\f0 eletype\f1  Model 33\f0  [and no \f1\tab\f0 storage device].  [The Syracuse University PDP-8 computer lab\par
\f1\tab\f0 had an odd collection of machines including one with neither a \f1\tab\f0 paper-tape\f1  \f0 reader nor a DECtape storage \f1 device\f0 .  By loading into \f1\tab\f0 the receiving computer a\f1  \f0 BIN loader program [with mod\f1 ified \tab\f0 instructions to match the device code of the\f1  \f0 IPB, this machine \f1\tab\f0 was more useful in the shared environment.\par
\par
\f1\tab\f0 TRAN is a\f1  \f0 stand-alone program that can be loaded by any operating \f1\tab\f0 system.  [TRAN was run\f1  \f0 from P?S/8 on a 4K PDP-8 with TC01/TU55 \f1\tab\f0 DECtape and the high-speed\f1  \f0 reader/punch and the server side of \f1\tab\f0 the IPB.]\page\cf3\f2 Footnotes [continued].\par
\cf0\f0\par
\f1\tab\f0 Charles Lasner used the IPB to allow a PDP-8/E equipped with a \f1\tab\f0 VT8E to control\f1  \f0 a LINC-8 by modifying PROGOFOP to support the IPB \f1\tab\f0 instead of the device 03\f1  \f0 keyboard\f1  of a Teletype Model 33\f0 .  [\f1 On \tab the \f0 LINC-8\f1 ,\f0  pure LINC mode programs do not support the\f1\tab\f0 teleprinter.]\par
\par
\f1\tab\f0 Eventually, the IPB was used to provide device support between \f1\tab\f0 two machines that\f1  \f0 have different storage devices; this allowed \f1\tab\f0 each to have access to the storage\f1  \f0 device of the other.  A common \f1\tab\f0 server program was written to be used on the\f1  \f0 storage-providing \f1\tab [server] \f0 side of the dual interface while device handlers were \f1\tab\f0 used on\f1  \f0 the o\f1 ther\f0  side.\par
\par
\f1\tab\f0 Note: There are bootable IBP-based systems for P?S/8 [and OS/8 \f1\tab\f0 can also be\f1  \f0 supported on 8K or larger machines].  Had this system \f1\tab\f0 been available at the time\f1  \f0 the TRAN program was in use, TRAN \f1\tab\f0 would never have been required.]  [Non-system\f1  \f0 handlers\f1  also\f0  exist \f1\tab\f0 for OS/8 IPB access.]\par
\par
